# One-time projection-fidelity transition (remove after re-baseline).
#
# The v1.5.0 baseline openapi.yaml asset was generated by the earlier, lossy CUE
# projection. This PR makes the projection faithful: it now emits the enum
# constraints CUE always enforced and rewrites hidden strict-variant definitions
# (#_AssessmentLogStrict, etc.) to their visible base schemas. oasdiff reports the
# gap between the old asset and the faithful projection as breaking, but the
# underlying schema contract is unchanged (0 ERR at the pre-converter-fix commit).
#
# These exceptions cover ONLY that transition. Once this PR merges and the next v1
# release publishes a faithful openapi.yaml, the baseline matches the projection
# and a follow-up PR MUST delete this file.

# Hidden strict-variant definition no longer projected as its own path (rewritten
# to its visible base schema).
api-path-removed-without-deprecation _AssessmentLogStrict

# Enum constraints now emitted by the projection (CUE always enforced them).
request-body-became-enum ArtifactType
request-body-became-enum ConfidenceLevel
request-body-became-enum EntityType
request-body-became-enum Lifecycle
request-body-became-enum Result
request-property-became-enum AssessmentLog
request-property-became-enum AssessmentRequirement
request-property-became-enum Catalog
request-property-became-enum Control
request-property-became-enum ControlCatalog
request-property-became-enum ControlEvaluation
request-property-became-enum Entity
request-property-became-enum EvaluationLog
request-property-became-enum Log
request-property-became-enum Metadata

# Required fields and types surfaced by rewriting hidden strict variants to their
# visible base schemas.
new-required-request-property ControlEvaluation
new-required-request-property EvaluationLog
request-property-type-changed ControlEvaluation
request-property-type-changed EvaluationLog
response-property-type-changed ControlEvaluation
response-property-type-changed EvaluationLog

# AssessmentRequirement gained `source` (an EntryMapping to an external
# requirement) as an alternative to inline `text`; exactly one of the two is
# now required, enforced by #_AssessmentRequirementStrict. `text` therefore
# became optional in the projection. Every existing v1 document still validates
# (all carry `text`), but consumers that assumed `text` is always present must
# also handle `source`.
response-property-became-optional AssessmentRequirement
response-property-became-optional Control
response-property-became-optional ControlCatalog
